.max-w-3xl.mx-auto.px-4.py-12
  %h1.text-3xl.font-bold.text-gray-900.mb-8 Help & Documentation

  %section.mb-10
    %h2.text-xl.font-bold.text-gray-900.mb-4 Getting Started
    
    .space-y-6
      %div
        %h3.font-bold.text-gray-900 1. Browse Cars
        %p.text-gray-600.text-sm Navigate to the Cars page to view all available car advertisements. You can sort by price, year, or mileage, and use pagination to browse through listings.
        
      %div
        %h3.font-bold.text-gray-900 2. Search for Specific Cars
        %p.text-gray-600.text-sm Use the Search page to filter cars by make, model, year range, and price range. This allows you to quickly find cars that match your criteria.
        
      %div
        %h3.font-bold.text-gray-900 3. Create an Account
        %p.text-gray-600.text-sm Sign up for an account to save your searches and access them later. This is useful if you're actively looking for a car and want to track specific criteria.

  %section.mb-10
    %h2.text-xl.font-bold.text-gray-900.mb-6 Frequently Asked Questions
    
    .space-y-8
      .border-b.border-gray-100.pb-6
        %h3.font-bold.text-gray-900.mb-2 How do I save a search?
        %p.text-gray-600.text-sm You must be logged in to save searches. After performing a search, click the "Save Search" button to store your search criteria.
        
      .border-b.border-gray-100.pb-6
        %h3.font-bold.text-gray-900.mb-2 How do I sort the car listings?
        %p.text-gray-600.text-sm On the Cars page, use the dropdown menu to select a sorting option. You can sort by price (low to high or high to low), year, or mileage.
        
      .border-b.border-gray-100.pb-6
        %h3.font-bold.text-gray-900.mb-2 How many results are shown per page?
        %p.text-gray-600.text-sm By default, 10 results are shown per page. Use the pagination controls at the bottom of the page to navigate through additional results.
        
      .pb-6
        %h3.font-bold.text-gray-900.mb-2 Is this a real car marketplace?
        %p.text-gray-600.text-sm No, this is a learning project demonstrating Rails and Tailwind CSS integration. All data is for demonstration purposes only.

  .bg-gray-50.rounded-lg.p-6.border.border-gray-100.mb-8
    %h3.font-bold.text-gray-900.mb-2 Need More Help?
    %p.text-gray-600.text-sm This is a demo application for learning purposes. For questions about implementation, refer to the Rails documentation or the project README.

  .mt-8
    = back_to_home_button
    